title ALES92 — Lotus's Schmitt trigger, the hysteresis comparator that gives ALES89's square a memory against chatter
prompt recur baton prin — take the next agent-doable Lindy-first crux-first lap, self-approve the design round, send each finished increment to origin and xykj61, stop at custody gates
think ALES91 (the DC blocker) named three candidate successors: a hysteresis comparator giving ALES89's square a memory against chatter, a carried-state shelving IIR, or a fresh DSP family. Crux-first, the Schmitt trigger is the hardest-still-tractable and highest-Lindy of the three: it is the FIRST comparator in the suite to carry state, so it inherits ALES91's split-equals-whole discipline where the memoryless infinite clipper could not, and a Schmitt trigger is a permanent staple — the debounce at the front of every gate, trigger, tempo-tap, and zero-cross. No custody gate: a bounded in-process i16 clip carrying one bit, siloed to lotus/.
think The map: if LOW and x ≥ t_high → flip HIGH; if HIGH and x ≤ t_low → flip LOW; otherwise hold. Output = +sample_max on the high rail, −sample_max on the low — ALES89's two rails, odd about the band, so no saturate is owed (both are legal i16 by construction). The band [t_low, t_high] is the hysteresis: a signal that only dithers inside it never flips, however noisy. The crux is that hysteresis carries ONE BIT (which rail), so exactly as ALES91's carried DC blocker a span compared in two pieces (the second continuing the first's ending rail) equals the whole compared once byte-for-byte, no spurious flip at the seam. That is what makes ALES92 the carried-state SIBLING of the memoryless infinite clipper rather than a copy.
think The from-silence convention is the LOW rail (high = false): before the signal has risen past t_high even once it has not triggered, so it reads low — stated plainly in doc, module, and log so the fresh SchmittTrigger and the from-silence schmitt cannot drift (the from-silence form is the default-state case of one carried implementation, mirroring ALES91's dc_block being the state=0 case of dc_block_carry).
think The coefficient law is its OWN: two SIGNED thresholds (not a magnitude like the comparators) ordered inside the rails, sample_min ≤ t_low ≤ t_high ≤ sample_max. t_low = t_high is LEGAL — the zero-width band, the plain memoryless comparator (chattering exactly at the shared level, a hard sign comparator everywhere else), the degenerate this rung reduces to exactly as ALES91's R = 0 is the legal first difference; t_low > t_high is an inverted, meaningless band and refuses BadThreshold. The witness proves the reason-it-exists law by contrast: hysteresis holds through a dither with ZERO flips where a single-threshold comparator on the same dither chatters flip after flip.
obs Followed the ALES91/ALES89 pattern exactly: standalone module (schmitt.rye importing timeline) + self-approved design read + witness + README status-line and rung-bullet sync + session-log-index row + this log, one signed round. Three faces of one implementation (schmitt_carry general, schmitt the from-silence case, SchmittTrigger the held value) mirror ALES91's dc_block_carry/dc_block/DcBlocker. Ten laws proven; the witness contrasts the hysteresis against an inline single-threshold comparator to prove the chatter distinction beside the map. Selftest GREEN, tame_style_check bans clean, schmitt.rye carries no ratchet debt (many asserts each with an invariant comment, snake_case, no @memcpy, i32 compare with i16 rails, no saturate owed).
loom witness=ales_schmitt_witness selftest=GREEN laws=10 module_lines=290 rails=2
file lotus/schmitt.rye the Schmitt trigger — flip high on a rise past t_high, low on a fall past t_low, hold between; one carried bit, split-equals-whole, ten laws proven
file tools/ales_schmitt_witness.rish builds the module, runs the selftest, asserts the single GREEN ales-schmitt line
file active-designing/20260814-224452_fill-ales92-lotus-schmitt-trigger.md the self-approved design read naming the crux, the carried-state sibling relation, the own band law, and the ten laws
file lotus/README.md front-door status line and a new rung bullet synced with ALES92, stamp refreshed
file session-logs/README.md newest-first index row prepended for ALES92
recommend keep-going the comparator family now stands on both signals — the memoryless infinite clipper for the clean, the hysteresis trigger for the noisy; the loop names its own next Lotus crux (a zero-crossing counter reading the trigger's flips as a pitch estimate, a timed debounce giving the band a time constant, a gate keyed on the trigger, or a fresh DSP family) as its own self-approved design round
